ED='2024'
S='TxDOT Standard Specifications, 2024, Item 468 Thermoplastic Pipe (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-tx-plastic-1','TX','Texas TxDOT thermoplastic pipe (HDPE, PP, PVC): backfill, mandrel and deflection limits (Item 468)',
"Texas (TxDOT 2024 Standard Specifications, Item 468, Thermoplastic Pipe). Bedding at least 4 inches thick, 6 inches where large rocks are present (468.3). Granular backfill goes in uniform loose layers about 6 inches deep up to 12 inches above the pipe; within 12 inches of the pipe use only hand-operated tampers; with flowable backfill the trench is pipe outside diameter plus 12 inches, the fill is carried at least 12 inches above the pipe, and you wait 24 hours before backfilling the rest (468.3.11). Stop backfilling if measured deflection passes 5 percent. No heavy earth-moving equipment over the pipe until at least 4 feet of compacted fill is in place (468.3.12). Final inspection (468.4.1): at least 30 days after backfill is complete, pull a mandrel sized at 95 percent of the pipe diameter through the whole length; if it will not pass, a 92.5 percent mandrel is tried and a remote camera is used to look at joints, cracks, deflection and ponding. Pipe deflected more than 7.5 percent of nominal diameter must be fixed or replaced (468.4.2). Joints: the bell must overlap at least two corrugations of the spigot.",S,U,ED)
S='TxDOT Standard Specifications, 2024, Items 465, 471, 476, 479 (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-tx-bore-1','TX','Texas TxDOT jacking, boring and tunneling pipe; manholes and inlets (Items 476, 465, 479)',
"Texas (TxDOT 2024 Standard Specifications). Item 476, Jacking, Boring, or Tunneling Pipe or Box: line and grade may not vary more than 1 inch in 10 feet; over-excavation no more than 2 inches at the top and sides, and anything over 1 inch is pressure grouted; do not excavate more than 2 feet ahead of the pipe; keep jacking going without interruption so the pipe does not set up; parallel jacked or tunneled lines need at least 3 feet clear between them; use plywood cushions between pipe ends, 1/2 inch minimum for pipe 30 inches and smaller and 3/4 inch for larger pipe and boxes; boring starts with a 2-inch pilot hole; keep a 3:1 slope from the edge of pavement on the shaft side. Item 465, Junction Boxes, Manholes, and Inlets: structures with rubber boots, gaskets or preformed sealant joints can be backfilled right away; place and compact backfill so the structure does not move. Item 479, adjusting manholes and inlets: flexible extension rings no taller than 3 inches; when capping, remove the structure to at least 1 foot below subgrade. Item 471 castings are load tested at 40,000 lb on a 9 by 9 inch block for 1 minute.",S,U,ED)
